.Dd October 1, 2026
.Dt GOLDOUT 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm goldout
.Nd Join AppleDouble files back onto their data files as two-fork files
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl h , Fl \-help
.Op Fl q , Fl \-quiet
.Op Fl n , Fl \-nolegacy
.Op Fl \-nosetinfo
.Op Fl \-nodelete
.Op Fl \-norecurse
.Op Fl \-version
.Op Ar PATH ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Goldout is the counterpart to
.Xr SplitForks 1
or
.Xr goldin 1 .
It exists because in macOS Sierra and later the
Apple-provided /System/Library/CoreServices/FixupResourceForks is missing.
.Pp
Goldout accepts directories or files as arguments.
It will recursively traverse any directory passed to it looking for
AppleDouble files.
When an AppleDouble file is found (or is passed as an argument), if
there is a matching counterpart (data fork) file, goldout will unite the
two as one two-fork file whose resource fork can be accessed by Resource
Manager calls or via the ..namedfork/rsrc path method.
A resource fork in the AppleDouble file replaces any resource fork the data file
already has.
If the counterpart is a folder, only its Finder information is restored.
.Pp
Processed AppleDouble files will be deleted unless the
.Fl \-nodelete
option is passed.
.Pp
If an AppleDouble file cannot be processed, goldout reports the error, leaves
the file in place and carries on; it then exits with status 1 when it has
finished.
Folders that cannot be read, including a
.Ar PATH
itself, are reported and skipped.
If a
.Ar PATH
cannot be processed at all (for example, it does not exist or is on an
unsupported file system), goldout reports the error and stops without
processing the remaining paths.
.Pp
If no
.Ar PATH
is given, goldout processes the whole boot volume, starting at
.Pa / .
This matches the behaviour of FixupResourceForks.
Use
.Fl n
or
.Fl \-nolegacy
to make a missing
.Ar PATH
an error instead.
.Pp
.Nm
accepts these flags and arguments:
.Bl -tag -width -indent
.It Fl h , Fl \-help
Print usage information and exit.
.It Fl q , Fl \-quiet
Do not list the AppleDouble files as they are processed.
Errors are still reported on standard error.
.It Fl n , Fl \-nolegacy
Don't default to
.Pa /
when no
.Ar PATH
is given; report an error and exit instead.
To make this the default, add an alias such as
.Dl alias goldout='goldout -n'
to your shell start-up file.
.It Fl \-nosetinfo
Don't restore the Finder information (such as type, creator and Finder flags)
from the AppleDouble file.
.It Fl \-nodelete
Don't delete the AppleDouble file after adding the resource fork and metadata
to the counterpart (data fork) file.
.It Fl \-norecurse
Only examine the AppleDouble files directly inside each
.Ar PATH ;
don't descend into its subdirectories.
.It Fl \-version
Print the tool's version and exit.
.It Ar PATH ...
One or more directories or files to examine.
If omitted, processing starts at
.Pa /
unless
.Fl n
or
.Fl \-nolegacy
is passed.
Files passed as arguments must be the AppleDouble encoded part of a file or
folder pair, and their names must begin with
.Ql \&._ .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width -indent
.It Pa /usr/local/bin/goldout
The installed tool.
.It example
Data fork file.
.It \._example
AppleDouble encoded resource fork and metadata.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
Success.
.It 1
One or more AppleDouble files could not be processed, or a
.Ar PATH
could not be processed.
.It 2
An unknown option was given, or no
.Ar PATH
was given with
.Fl n .
.El
.Sh NOTES
Goldout works on HFS, HFS+ and APFS volumes.
It fails with an error on any other file system.
.Pp
Goldout lives here:
.Lk https://github.com/packagesdev/goldout .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr FixupResourceForks 1 ,
.Xr goldin 1 ,
.Xr SplitForks 1
.Sh STANDARDS
RFC 1740 documents AppleSingle/AppleDouble formats.
